# Who is asked to look at what.
#
# One maintainer today. This file names them rather than a team, because a
# CODEOWNERS entry pointing at a team that does not exist is silently inert:
# no review is ever requested and nothing says so. Replace these with a team
# handle the day there is a team, not before.
#
# A warning worth keeping here, for whoever enables branch protection. GitHub
# will not let anyone approve their own pull request. So turning on "require
# review from Code Owners" while a single person owns everything blocks that
# person from merging anything of their own. Leave it off until there are two
# maintainers, or keep the administrator bypass. The value of this file in
# the meantime is that outside contributions land in front of someone
# automatically.

# Default owner for everything.
*                           @Coopyrightdmin

# Paths where a mistake is not merely a bug: the signed wire format, the
# verification path, key handling, and the plugin boundary.
/src/crypto/                @Coopyrightdmin
/src/keys.rs                @Coopyrightdmin
/src/verify.rs              @Coopyrightdmin
/src/storage/receipt_format.rs @Coopyrightdmin

# The hashing rules and the invariants that guard them. Both decide what a
# receipt means; changing either silently is how a guarantee stops being one.
/src/hashing.rs             @Coopyrightdmin
/src/storage/causal_ledger.rs @Coopyrightdmin
/tests/security_invariants.rs @Coopyrightdmin
/tools/mutation-gate.sh     @Coopyrightdmin

# Release and supply-chain configuration.
/.github/workflows/         @Coopyrightdmin
/deny.toml                  @Coopyrightdmin
/LICENSE                    @Coopyrightdmin
/NOTICE                     @Coopyrightdmin
